24,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
25,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,It seems our reporting process is heavily burdened by physical assets. Hardware requires outside appraisals that delay our audits significantly.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,We have a bottleneck. Our recruiters are great for office roles but struggle immensely with field and supervisory staff.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"Interestingly, our most stable returns and best retention come from specialized tools, while operational-heavy models have been our downfall.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"We are burning through reserves faster than planned, and our credit line is useless for subscription-based security.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Shion,,Security reviews for medical or financial data are taking three times longer than other deployments. Hardware is also prone to supply shocks.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Misaki, if the credit line doesn't support subscriptions, we need to be careful about the revenue model of the next seed.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, does that mean we should avoid companies requiring specialized field crews or complex hardware?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"I agree. The data suggests that ""quiet"" back-office tools are our safest bet for actual exits.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"Exactly. We need something that doesn't demand immediate, heavy follow-on capital or rely on unbilled invoices for credit.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Shion,,And something that doesn't get stuck in a nine-month security review or a chip shortage.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Jonathan, you mentioned the adviser bench. Is there any capacity to help a new company with logistics?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"The logistics advisers are currently idle, but the software partners are completely maxed out on board seats.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"If we pick a software company, who will actually guide them if the partners are full?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Misaki,,That's a fair point. We might need a balance between our capacity and the company's needs.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Shion,,Logic suggests we avoid medical software if we can't afford the deployment delay.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"We need a company that is easy to audit, easy to report, and doesn't break our bank.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,And one where we can actually fill the necessary roles quickly.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,4,talk,Shizue,,Let's hope the candidates align with these constraints.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I'm looking for low capital intensity and high creditability.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,4,talk,Shion,,I'm looking for a fast path to the first customer.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
