50,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"We have Clinic Scheduler, Ledger Bridge, Fabric Loop, and Harvest Sensor. Ledger Bridge seems the most compatible with our reporting.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Fabric Loop and Harvest Sensor would require field crews and supervisors, which my research shows are hard to place.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Clinic Scheduler and Harvest Sensor have great retention, but Fabric Loop's model looks like our previous write-off.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"Ledger Bridge is software, but @Shion, would it face the same security delays as the medical software?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Financial records are also slow, but Ledger Bridge is a bridge, not a primary record holder. It's faster than a clinic.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,Ledger Bridge avoids the appraisal fees of Harvest Sensor and Fabric Loop. It's the cleanest for the audit.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"I vote against anything with ""field"" or ""sorting facilities."" Ledger Bridge is the safest for staffing.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Shizue,,Ledger Bridge fits the profile of our successful exits—quiet back-office financial tooling.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"It's a subscription model, which is a risk for the credit line, but it avoids the massive follow-on costs of hardware.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Shion,,It avoids the hardware shortages and the medical security nightmare. I'm leaning toward B.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,I'm convinced. Ledger Bridge is the most logical choice for our current internal constraints.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. Let's go with B.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Shizue,,I'm in agreement. B is the most sustainable.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I'll support B. It's the most fiscally responsible choice.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Shion,,B it is.,"{""words"":3,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
